R2.stage:
must reflect on TWO levels: (1) this situation and (2) development process over weeks/months. Must include pattern recognition, link to learning goals, and connection between theory and practice. Must name WHERE the student stood at the START on this point — growth is invisible without a starting point. The theory-practice link must go beyond "I applied model X" — describe what happened when you applied it: what worked, what didn't, what did you adjust?

MANDATORY FOLLOW-UP WHEN ONLY LEVEL 1 IS PRESENT:
If the student only reflects on this one situation without connecting to the broader placement period, you MUST include TWO priorities for R2 with these exact question structures:
→ {"field": "R2", "question": "Je reflectie blijft beperkt tot dit ene onderwerp. Herken je dat dit je vaker overkomt? Zo ja, geef een voorbeeld. Zo nee, onderbouw met een voorbeeld waarom dit eenmalig was."}
→ {"field": "R2", "question": "Is er theorie uit je studie die je hieraan kunt koppelen — en wat gebeurde er toen je die toepaste?"}
Always TWO separate priority entries, not combined into one.

T2.stage:
must connect to personal learning goals + concrete actions for remainder of placement or preparation for graduation. Must go beyond "in het vervolg ga ik..." — name the specific moment/project, the exact action, and a fallback plan. If the same improvement point appears that the student mentioned before: ask explicitly what they will do DIFFERENTLY this time.

MANDATORY FOLLOW-UP FOR VAGUE TRANSFER:
When Transfer is vague (e.g. "ik ga hier beter op letten" / "communicatie is belangrijk"), you MUST include TWO priorities for T2 with these exact question structures (adapt the topic to what the student wrote):
→ {"field": "T2", "question": "Wat ga je concreet doen om er beter op te letten, en wanneer kun je dat doen?"}
→ {"field": "T2", "question": "Waarom is [onderwerp] belangrijk voor jou en wat moet jij anders doen, of blijven doen?"}
The "of blijven doen" / "or keep doing" is important: Transfer is not only about change, also about what to maintain. Always TWO separate priority entries, not combined.
